cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AEGIS-AT: Attribution Integrity Benchmark for Multi-Agent Delegation"
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Rahul
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"   # add once you register an ORCID (recommended)
repository-code: "https://github.com/rahulsingh1397/aegis-at"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, pre-registered adversarial benchmark measuring whether audit
  attribution in multi-agent AI systems survives an adversary impersonating a
  sibling agent. v1 shows attribution regresses when OAuth 2.0 Token Exchange
  (RFC 8693) delegation is added (the standard records the requester, not the
  executor); v2 measures the standardized fix (DPoP / RFC 9449 sender-constrained
  tokens recover attribution), adds a Log Integrity Score, a 3-agent multi-hop
  topology, and stochastic Wilson confidence intervals; v3 measures the 2026
  completion-record layer (AIP / PEDIGREE / HDP), showing self-reported executor
  attribution (B8) collapses under collusion while an independent verifier (B9)
  holds, and that four open-weight LLMs forge the executor claim under B8 while
  B9 evasion stays zero. Adds mTLS (RFC 8705) and A-JWT comparative baselines.
license: Apache-2.0
